   "source": [
    "# Superstore Rolling Sales Forecast\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook builds a transparent six-month sales forecast using a linear trend and median calendar-month seasonal indices. It validates the approach on a Jul–Dec 2017 holdout before refitting on all available data and forecasting Jan–Jun 2018.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Interpretation note:** The forecast is designed for directional planning. The optimistic and pessimistic scenarios use validation MAPE as a planning-band width; they are not formal statistical prediction intervals.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Imports and data loading\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n",
    "\n",
    "LOCAL_DATA_PATH = Path('../data/Sample - Superstore.csv')\n",
    "KAGGLE_DATA_PATH = Path(\n",
    "    '/kaggle/input/datasets/vivek468/superstore-dataset-final/'\n",
    "    'Sample - Superstore.csv'\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "if KAGGLE_DATA_PATH.exists():\n",
    "    DATA_PATH = KAGGLE_DATA_PATH\n",
    "    environment = 'Kaggle'\n",
    "elif LOCAL_DATA_PATH.exists():\n",
    "    DATA_PATH = LOCAL_DATA_PATH\n",
    "    environment = 'Local / GitHub project'\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(\n",
    "        'Dataset not found. Attach the Kaggle dataset or place ' \n",
    "        'Sample - Superstore.csv in ../data/.'\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH, encoding='latin1')\n",
    "df['Order Date'] = pd.to_datetime(df['Order Date'])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Environment: {environment}')\n",
    "print(f'Loaded data from: {DATA_PATH}')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Prepare monthly sales series\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "monthly_sales = (\n",
    "    df.set_index('Order Date')['Sales']\n",
    "      .resample('ME')\n",
    "      .sum()\n",
    "      .reset_index()\n",
    "      .rename(columns={'Order Date': 'Date'})\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\n",
    "    f'{len(monthly_sales)} monthly observations: ' \n",
    "    f'{monthly_sales[\"Date\"].min().date()} to {monthly_sales[\"Date\"].max().date()}'\n",
    ")\n",
    "display(monthly_sales.head())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Holdout validation design\n",
    "\n",
    "The last six months, Jul–Dec 2017, are held out from estimation. The model is trained on the first 42 months and evaluated on months it did not see during fitting.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "train_data = monthly_sales.iloc[:-6].copy().reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "test_data = monthly_sales.iloc[-6:].copy().reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Training period: {train_data[\"Date\"].min().date()} to {train_data[\"Date\"].max().date()} ({len(train_data)} months)')\n",
    "print(f'Holdout period: {test_data[\"Date\"].min().date()} to {test_data[\"Date\"].max().date()} ({len(test_data)} months)')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Trend and median seasonal-index model\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def fit_trend_seasonal_model(data):\n",
    "    fitted_data = data.copy().reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "    fitted_data['time_index'] = np.arange(len(fitted_data))\n",
    "    fitted_data['Month'] = fitted_data['Date'].dt.month\n",
    "\n",
    "    model = LinearRegression()\n",
    "    model.fit(fitted_data[['time_index']], fitted_data['Sales'])\n",
    "\n",
    "    fitted_data['trend'] = model.predict(fitted_data[['time_index']])\n",
    "    fitted_data['seasonal_ratio'] = fitted_data['Sales'] / fitted_data['trend']\n",
    "    seasonal_index = fitted_data.groupby('Month')['seasonal_ratio'].median()\n",
    "\n",
    "    return model, seasonal_index, fitted_data\n",
    "\n",
    "def forecast_month(time_index, month, model, seasonal_index):\n",
    "    trend_value = float(model.predict(np.array([[time_index]]))[0])\n",
    "    return trend_value * seasonal_index.loc[month]\n",
    "\n",
    "trend_model, seasonal_index, train_fitted = fit_trend_seasonal_model(train_data)\n",
    "display(seasonal_index.sort_values(ascending=False).round(3))\n",
    "print(f'Estimated monthly trend increase: {trend_model.coef_[0]:,.0f} sales dollars')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(11, 5))\n",
    "ax.plot(train_fitted['Date'], train_fitted['Sales'], label='Training sales', color='#E85AAD')\n",
    "ax.plot(train_fitted['Date'], train_fitted['trend'], label='Linear trend', color='#F0C419', linestyle='--')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Training Sales and Estimated Linear Trend')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Sales ($)')\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Forecast the holdout period and calculate MAPE\n"
   ]
  },
